# Keep every text file LF in the repository and in working trees.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which checks
# files out with CRLF. gofmt requires LF, so every freshly checked-out .go file
# is reported as unformatted until it happens to be rewritten by an editor.
#
# Attributes take precedence over core.autocrlf, so this fixes the working tree
# on every machine without asking contributors to change their Git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
